  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           8834 1451   72
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         8834 1451   73
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR8834 1451   74
       expands from 0 to 4.999853E+3 eV. A total of               8834 1451   75
       2 l-values are used and 344 resonances. The resonance      8834 1451   76
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              8834 1451   77
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       8834 1451   78
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          8834 1451   79
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     8834 1451   80
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    8834 1451   81
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  8834 1451   82
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   8834 1451   83
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          8834 1451   84
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       8834 1451   85
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    8834 1451   86
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       8834 1451   87
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         8834 1451   88
       The s-wave average level spacing is 30.77 eV and           8834 1451   89
       the s-wave neutron strength is 3.983e-05 1e-4.             8834 1451   90
                                                                  8834 1451   91
       After the ladder method, the retroactive method is applied 8834 1451   92
       to update the MF32 and MF2 with the SAMMY code.            8834 1451   93
                                                                  8834 1451   94
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  8834 1451   95
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    8834 1451   96
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    8834 1451   97
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   8834 1451   98
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    8834 1451   99
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              8834 1451  100
        SAMMY is used in the retroactive mode to update MF32.     8834 1451  101
