***************************** T A L Y S **************************8834 1451  182
                                                                  8834 1451  183
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   8834 1451  184
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      8834 1451  185
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    8834 1451  186
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     8834 1451  187
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  8834 1451  188
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        8834 1451  189
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    8834 1451  190
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         8834 1451  191
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      8834 1451  192
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    8834 1451  193
stored in this data file:                                         8834 1451  194
                                                                  8834 1451  195
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   8834 1451  196
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     8834 1451  197
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 8834 1451  198
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   8834 1451  199
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                8834 1451  200
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   8834 1451  201
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    8834 1451  202
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        8834 1451  203
- Recoil data                                                     8834 1451  204
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           8834 1451  205
- Total particle energy spectra                                   8834 1451  206
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      8834 1451  207
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        8834 1451  208
- Residual production cross sections                              8834 1451  209
                                                                  8834 1451  210
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            8834 1451  211
parameterization we refer to [kon12]. If for this specific        8834 1451  212
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   8834 1451  213
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                8834 1451  214
                                                                  8834 1451  215
